<description>
Paint the empty gutters of a rectangular lattice of grey 2x2 blocks.

Input structure:
- The background is the most common color.
- The only foreground color forms a complete rectangular array of separated 2x2 blocks.
- Blank row bands and column bands between adjacent block bands are the lattice gutters.

Rule:
- Keep the grey blocks unchanged.
- Paint gutter background pixels red inside the foreground bounding rectangle.
- Paint gutter background pixels blue where the same gutter rows or columns extend outside that bounding rectangle.

Key insight:
- The grey blocks define row bands and column bands; their intervening blank bands are the lines to color, and the block-array bbox separates internal gutters from exterior extensions.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "summary": "Empty gutters between grey block rows and columns are colored red inside the block-array bbox and blue on exterior extensions.",
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "grey 2x2 block lattice on the background; blank row/column bands between adjacent block bands are gutters",
  "transform": "paint background pixels in gutter rows/columns red inside the lattice bbox and blue where those same gutter rows/columns extend outside the bbox"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 10x10 [observed]
  background: black (0)
  lattice:
    block_color: grey (5), sole foreground color
    block_size: 2x2, all identical
    row_bands: 2-3 groups of 2 consecutive rows [observed]; solver requires >=2
    col_bands: 2-3 groups of 2 consecutive cols [observed]; solver requires >=2
    completeness: every row_band x col_band intersection has a 2x2 block (full rectangular grid)
    row_gutter_widths: 1-2 each, between consecutive row bands
    col_gutter_widths: 1-2 each, between consecutive col bands
    gutters_may_vary: yes, widths need not be uniform within an axis (test_0 has col gutters 2,1)
  margins:
    top/bottom/left/right: 0-4 each; budget = grid_dim - n_bands*2 - sum(gutter_widths)
    total_margin: >=1 so blue paint appears [observed]
  transform:
    gutter_pixels_inside_bbox: painted red (2)
    gutter_pixels_outside_bbox: painted blue (1)
    grey_blocks: unchanged
    non_gutter_bg: unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (input-only; transform is deterministic)
  steps:
    1. Pick grid 10x10
    2. Choose n_row_bands in {2,3}, n_col_bands in {2,3}
    3. For each axis, choose gutter widths (each 1-2); compute margin = 10 - n_bands*2 - sum(gutters)
    4. Reject if margin < 0; split margin into before/after (>=0 each); ensure total margin across both axes >= 1
